    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-16ac",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16AC Reduction for cooperation with law enforcement agencies",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-16ac"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.17",
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if a court imposing a sentence, or making an\norder, for a federal offence:\n\n(a) reduces the severity of the sentence or order; or\n\n(b) reduces the non-parole period in relation to the sentence (if\napplicable);\nbecause the offender has undertaken to cooperate with law\nenforcement agencies in proceedings (including confiscation\nproceedings) relating to any offence.\n\n(2) The court must:\n\n(a) state that the sentence, order or non-parole period is being\nreduced for that reason; and\n\n(b) specify the sentence that would have been imposed, the order\nthat would have been made or the non-parole period that\nwould have been fixed but for that reduction.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 7  Sentencing and parole",
      "skos:definition": "(1) This section applies if a court imposing a sentence, or making an\norder, for a federal offence:\n\n(a) reduces the severity of the sentence or order; or\n\n(b) reduces the non-parole period in relation to the sentence (if\napplicable);\nbecause the offender has undertaken to cooperate with law\nenforcement agencies in proceedings (including confiscation\nproceedings) relating to any offence.\n\n(2) The court must:\n\n(a) state that the sentence, order or non-parole period is being\nreduced for that reason; and\n\n(b) specify the sentence that would have been imposed, the order\nthat would have been made or the non-parole period that\nwould have been fixed but for that reduction.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 7  Sentencing and parole",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-16ac-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-16ac-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0356ac5523cd2622dae368eb40dbe32dbd9777df72de6470931841e46d80dc69"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-16ac",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16AC Reduction for cooperation with law enforcement agencies",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 17,
      "values:originalText": "(1) This section applies if a court imposing a sentence, or making an\norder, for a federal offence:\n\n(a) reduces the severity of the sentence or order; or\n\n(b) reduces the non-parole period in relation to the sentence (if\napplicable);\nbecause the offender has undertaken to cooperate with law\nenforcement agencies in proceedings (including confiscation\nproceedings) relating to any offence.\n\n(2) The court must:\n\n(a) state that the sentence, order or non-parole period is being\nreduced for that reason; and\n\n(b) specify the sentence that would have been imposed, the order\nthat would have been made or the non-parole period that\nwould have been fixed but for that reduction.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 7  Sentencing and parole"
    },
