    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 Subsections 19AC(4) and (5)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(4) A court may decline to make a recognizance release order in\nrespect of a person if:\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that such an order is not appropriate,\nhaving regard to:\n\n(i) the nature and circumstances of the offence or offences\nconcerned; and\n\n(ii) the antecedents of the person; or\n\n(b) the person is expected to be serving a State or Territory\nsentence on the day after the end of the federal sentence, or\nthe last to be served of the federal sentences, as reduced by\nany remissions or reductions under section 19AA.\n\n(5) If the court declines to make a recognizance release order, the court\nmust:\n\n(a) state its reasons for so declining; and\n\n(b) cause the reasons to be entered in the records of the court.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSentencing and parole  Schedule 7\nNon-parole periods and recognizance release orders  Part 4\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\n\n(4) A court may decline to make a recognizance release order in\nrespect of a person if:\n\n(a) the court is satisfied that such an order is not appropriate,\nhaving regard to:\n\n(i) the nature and circumstances of the offence or offences\nconcerned; and\n\n(ii) the antecedents of the person; or\n\n(b) the person is expected to be serving a State or Territory\nsentence on the day after the end of the federal sentence, or\nthe last to be served of the federal sentences, as reduced by\nany remissions or reductions under section 19AA.\n\n(5) If the court declines to make a recognizance release order, the court\nmust:\n\n(a) state its reasons for so declining; and\n\n(b) cause the reasons to be entered in the records of the court.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSentencing and parole  Schedule 7\nNon-parole periods and recognizance release orders  Part 4\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-12-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-12-ss-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "45006b563b2fa2182b7ea81cca2aac16faa404d7946d1c0f51f91fbff6cf069d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-12",
