    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-19",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "19 Before section 19AL",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-19"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nSubdivision A—Release on parole or licence\n19AKA  Purposes of parole\n\nThe purposes of parole are the following:\n\n(a) the protection of the community;\n\n(b) the rehabilitation of the offender;\n\n(c) the reintegration of the offender into the community.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\nSubdivision A—Release on parole or licence\n19AKA  Purposes of parole\n\nThe purposes of parole are the following:\n\n(a) the protection of the community;\n\n(b) the rehabilitation of the offender;\n\n(c) the reintegration of the offender into the community.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-19-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-19-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2129e60206495682f681c732811a0a099dca5e10d010f02adcbc8fd0b24ce371",
      "skos:note": "Purposes of parole"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-19",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "19 Before section 19AL",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\nSubdivision A—Release on parole or licence\n19AKA  Purposes of parole\n\nThe purposes of parole are the following:\n\n(a) the protection of the community;\n\n(b) the rehabilitation of the offender;\n\n(c) the reintegration of the offender into the community."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-19-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-19"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-19-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "hasPurpose",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Defines the purpose of parole",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-20",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20 After section 19AL",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-20"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.26",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n19ALA  Matters that may be considered in decisions about parole\norders\n\n(1) In making a decision under section 19AL in relation to a person,\nthe Attorney-General may have regard to any of the following\nmatters that are known to the Attorney-General and relevant to the\ndecision:\n\n(a) the risk to the community of releasing the person on parole;\n\n(b) the person’s conduct while serving his or her sentence;\n\n(c) whether the person has satisfactorily completed programs\nordered by a court or recommended by the relevant State or\nTerritory corrective services or parole agency;\n\n(d) the likely effect on the victim, or victim’s family, of releasing\nthe person on parole;\n\n(e) the nature and circumstances of the offence to which the\nperson’s sentence relates;\n\n(f) any comments made by the sentencing court;\n\n(g) the person’s criminal history;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSentencing and parole  Schedule 7\nParole—general  Part 6\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(h) any report or information in relation to the granting of parole\nthat has been provided by the relevant State or Territory\ncorrective services or parole agency;\n\n(i) the behaviour of the person when subject to any previous\nparole order or licence;\n\n(j) the likelihood that the person will comply with the conditions\nof the parole order;\n\n(k) whether releasing the person on parole is likely to assist the\nperson to adjust to lawful community life;\n\n(l) whether the length of the parole period is sufficient to\nachieve the purposes of parole;\n\n(m) any special circumstances, including the likelihood that the\nperson will be subject to removal or deportation upon release.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not limit the matters that the Attorney-General\nmay consider in making a decision under section 19AL.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n19ALA  Matters that may be considered in decisions about parole\norders\n\n(1) In making a decision under section 19AL in relation to a person,\nthe Attorney-General may have regard to any of the following\nmatters that are known to the Attorney-General and relevant to the\ndecision:\n\n(a) the risk to the community of releasing the person on parole;\n\n(b) the person’s conduct while serving his or her sentence;\n\n(c) whether the person has satisfactorily completed programs\nordered by a court or recommended by the relevant State or\nTerritory corrective services or parole agency;\n\n(d) the likely effect on the victim, or victim’s family, of releasing\nthe person on parole;\n\n(e) the nature and circumstances of the offence to which the\nperson’s sentence relates;\n\n(f) any comments made by the sentencing court;\n\n(g) the person’s criminal history;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSentencing and parole  Schedule 7\nParole—general  Part 6\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(h) any report or information in relation to the granting of parole\nthat has been provided by the relevant State or Territory\ncorrective services or parole agency;\n\n(i) the behaviour of the person when subject to any previous\nparole order or licence;\n\n(j) the likelihood that the person will comply with the conditions\nof the parole order;\n\n(k) whether releasing the person on parole is likely to assist the\nperson to adjust to lawful community life;\n\n(l) whether the length of the parole period is sufficient to\nachieve the purposes of parole;\n\n(m) any special circumstances, including the likelihood that the\nperson will be subject to removal or deportation upon release.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not limit the matters that the Attorney-General\nmay consider in making a decision under section 19AL.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-20-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-20-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "30fd54505e2b5467f816250429a529f68d9ab41fa333eff46a7ce90b1aa5bf92"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-20",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20 After section 19AL",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 26,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n19ALA  Matters that may be considered in decisions about parole\norders\n\n(1) In making a decision under section 19AL in relation to a person,\nthe Attorney-General may have regard to any of the following\nmatters that are known to the Attorney-General and relevant to the\ndecision:\n\n(a) the risk to the community of releasing the person on parole;\n\n(b) the person’s conduct while serving his or her sentence;\n\n(c) whether the person has satisfactorily completed programs\nordered by a court or recommended by the relevant State or\nTerritory corrective services or parole agency;\n\n(d) the likely effect on the victim, or victim’s family, of releasing\nthe person on parole;\n\n(e) the nature and circumstances of the offence to which the\nperson’s sentence relates;\n\n(f) any comments made by the sentencing court;\n\n(g) the person’s criminal history;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSentencing and parole  Schedule 7\nParole—general  Part 6\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\n(h) any report or information in relation to the granting of parole\nthat has been provided by the relevant State or Territory\ncorrective services or parole agency;\n\n(i) the behaviour of the person when subject to any previous\nparole order or licence;\n\n(j) the likelihood that the person will comply with the conditions\nof the parole order;\n\n(k) whether releasing the person on parole is likely to assist the\nperson to adjust to lawful community life;\n\n(l) whether the length of the parole period is sufficient to\nachieve the purposes of parole;\n\n(m) any special circumstances, including the likelihood that the\nperson will be subject to removal or deportation upon release.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not limit the matters that the Attorney-General\nmay consider in making a decision under section 19AL."
    },
