    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Before section 19AQ",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n19APB  Effect of parole order and licence on sentence\n\n(1) If a parole order is made, or a licence is granted, in relation to a\nperson:\n\n(a) the person is taken to be still under sentence and not to have\nserved the part of any sentence that remained to be served at\nthe beginning of the parole period or licence period, until:\n\n(i) the parole period or licence period ends without the\nparole order or licence being revoked; or\n\n(ii) the person is otherwise discharged from imprisonment;\nand\n\n(b) the person is taken:\n\n(i) to have served the part of any sentence that remained to\nbe served at the beginning of the parole period or\nlicence period; and\n\n(ii) to have been discharged from imprisonment;\n\nif the parole period or licence period ends without the parole\norder or licence being revoked.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 7  Sentencing and parole",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n19APB  Effect of parole order and licence on sentence\n\n(1) If a parole order is made, or a licence is granted, in relation to a\nperson:\n\n(a) the person is taken to be still under sentence and not to have\nserved the part of any sentence that remained to be served at\nthe beginning of the parole period or licence period, until:\n\n(i) the parole period or licence period ends without the\nparole order or licence being revoked; or\n\n(ii) the person is otherwise discharged from imprisonment;\nand\n\n(b) the person is taken:\n\n(i) to have served the part of any sentence that remained to\nbe served at the beginning of the parole period or\nlicence period; and\n\n(ii) to have been discharged from imprisonment;\n\nif the parole period or licence period ends without the parole\norder or licence being revoked.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 7  Sentencing and parole",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-21-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-21-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4fb339fd827b7f202e79dabcb51e95b69142a51f12bbefb4e6ed6c1bf5864aa6",
      "skos:note": "Parole order and licence affect sentence duration"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Before section 19AQ",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n19APB  Effect of parole order and licence on sentence\n\n(1) If a parole order is made, or a licence is granted, in relation to a\nperson:\n\n(a) the person is taken to be still under sentence and not to have\nserved the part of any sentence that remained to be served at\nthe beginning of the parole period or licence period, until:\n\n(i) the parole period or licence period ends without the\nparole order or licence being revoked; or\n\n(ii) the person is otherwise discharged from imprisonment;\nand\n\n(b) the person is taken:\n\n(i) to have served the part of any sentence that remained to\nbe served at the beginning of the parole period or\nlicence period; and\n\n(ii) to have been discharged from imprisonment;\n\nif the parole period or licence period ends without the parole\norder or licence being revoked.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 7  Sentencing and parole"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-21-norm",
