    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-43",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "43 After subsection 20(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-43"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) If the court specifies under paragraph (1)(a) or (b), as mentioned in\nsubparagraph (1)(a)(iv), the condition that the person will, during\nthe specified period:\n\n(a) be subject to the supervision of a probation officer appointed\nin accordance with the order; and\n\n(b) obey all reasonable directions of the probation officer;\nthe court must also specify the condition that the person will not\ntravel interstate or overseas without the written permission of the\nprobation officer.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSentencing and parole  Schedule 7\nAlternative sentencing options  Part 11\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(1A) If the court specifies under paragraph (1)(a) or (b), as mentioned in\nsubparagraph (1)(a)(iv), the condition that the person will, during\nthe specified period:\n\n(a) be subject to the supervision of a probation officer appointed\nin accordance with the order; and\n\n(b) obey all reasonable directions of the probation officer;\nthe court must also specify the condition that the person will not\ntravel interstate or overseas without the written permission of the\nprobation officer.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSentencing and parole  Schedule 7\nAlternative sentencing options  Part 11\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-43-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-43-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "39bfa5653dcfc25b9d663aa54574a3540f899b21540a44fe08c7b7c2a4401df6",
      "skos:note": "Restrict travel without permission"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-43",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "43 After subsection 20(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(1A) If the court specifies under paragraph (1)(a) or (b), as mentioned in\nsubparagraph (1)(a)(iv), the condition that the person will, during\nthe specified period:\n\n(a) be subject to the supervision of a probation officer appointed\nin accordance with the order; and\n\n(b) obey all reasonable directions of the probation officer;\nthe court must also specify the condition that the person will not\ntravel interstate or overseas without the written permission of the\nprobation officer.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSentencing and parole  Schedule 7\nAlternative sentencing options  Part 11\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015"
    },
    {
