    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-46",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46 Subsection 20AB(1)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-46"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) A court may pass a sentence, or make an order, in respect of a\nperson convicted before the court in a participating State or\nparticipating Territory of a federal offence, if:\n\n(a) subsection (1AA) applies to the sentence or order; and\n\n(b) under the law of the State or Territory, a court is empowered\nto pass such a sentence, or make such an order, in respect of a\nState or Territory offender in corresponding cases; and\n\n(c) the first-mentioned court is:\n\n(i) empowered as mentioned in paragraph (b); or\n\n(ii) a federal court.\n\n(1AA) This subsection applies to a sentence or order that is:\n\n(a) known as any of the following:\n\n(i) an attendance centre order or attendance order;\n\n(ii) a community based order;\n\n(iii) a community correction order;\n\n(iv) a community custody order;\n\n(v) a community service order;\n\n(vi) a community work order;\n\n(vii) a drug or alcohol treatment order or rehabilitation order;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 7  Sentencing and parole",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) A court may pass a sentence, or make an order, in respect of a\nperson convicted before the court in a participating State or\nparticipating Territory of a federal offence, if:\n\n(a) subsection (1AA) applies to the sentence or order; and\n\n(b) under the law of the State or Territory, a court is empowered\nto pass such a sentence, or make such an order, in respect of a\nState or Territory offender in corresponding cases; and\n\n(c) the first-mentioned court is:\n\n(i) empowered as mentioned in paragraph (b); or\n\n(ii) a federal court.\n\n(1AA) This subsection applies to a sentence or order that is:\n\n(a) known as any of the following:\n\n(i) an attendance centre order or attendance order;\n\n(ii) a community based order;\n\n(iii) a community correction order;\n\n(iv) a community custody order;\n\n(v) a community service order;\n\n(vi) a community work order;\n\n(vii) a drug or alcohol treatment order or rehabilitation order;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 7  Sentencing and parole",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-46-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-7-sec-46-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "34afcfdcaae911b88b3f7f3f86ff6ca38b964c91db24e1f6ce8acf1e5afa3d6b",
      "skos:note": "A court may pass a sentence or make an order in respect of a person convicted before the court in a participating State or Territory of a federal offence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-7-sec-46",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "46 Subsection 20AB(1)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 35,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) A court may pass a sentence, or make an order, in respect of a\nperson convicted before the court in a participating State or\nparticipating Territory of a federal offence, if:\n\n(a) subsection (1AA) applies to the sentence or order; and\n\n(b) under the law of the State or Territory, a court is empowered\nto pass such a sentence, or make such an order, in respect of a\nState or Territory offender in corresponding cases; and\n\n(c) the first-mentioned court is:\n\n(i) empowered as mentioned in paragraph (b); or\n\n(ii) a federal court.\n\n(1AA) This subsection applies to a sentence or order that is:\n\n(a) known as any of the following:\n\n(i) an attendance centre order or attendance order;\n\n(ii) a community based order;\n\n(iii) a community correction order;\n\n(iv) a community custody order;\n\n(v) a community service order;\n\n(vi) a community work order;\n\n(vii) a drug or alcohol treatment order or rehabilitation order;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 7  Sentencing and parole"
    },
