    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-11-sec-12",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "12 At the end of section 32",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-11-sec-12"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nDeciding to take no further action\n\n(8) The Integrity Commissioner may decide under subsection (2) to\ntake no further action in relation to the corruption issue only if he\nor she is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the corruption issue is already being, or will be, investigated\nby:\n\n(i) a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(ii) a government agency; or\n\n(iii) an integrity agency for a State or Territory; or\n\n(b) the corrupt conduct to which the corruption issue relates has\nbeen, is or will be, the subject of proceedings before a court;\nor\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 11  Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 153, 2015\n\n(c) an investigation of the corruption issue is not warranted\nhaving regard to all the circumstances.\n\n(9) The Integrity Commissioner must advise the head of the law\nenforcement agency of a decision under subsection (2) to take no\nfurther action in relation to the corruption issue. That advice must\nbe given:\n\n(a) in writing; and\n\n(b) as soon as reasonably practicable after the decision is made.\n\n(10) This Act continues to apply to the head of the law enforcement\nagency, and that agency, in relation to the corruption issue unless\nthe Integrity Commissioner advises otherwise:\n\n(a) in the advice given under subsection (9); or\n\n(b) in a later written advice given to the head of that agency.",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\nDeciding to take no further action\n\n(8) The Integrity Commissioner may decide under subsection (2) to\ntake no further action in relation to the corruption issue only if he\nor she is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the corruption issue is already being, or will be, investigated\nby:\n\n(i) a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(ii) a government agency; or\n\n(iii) an integrity agency for a State or Territory; or\n\n(b) the corrupt conduct to which the corruption issue relates has\nbeen, is or will be, the subject of proceedings before a court;\nor\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 11  Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 153, 2015\n\n(c) an investigation of the corruption issue is not warranted\nhaving regard to all the circumstances.\n\n(9) The Integrity Commissioner must advise the head of the law\nenforcement agency of a decision under subsection (2) to take no\nfurther action in relation to the corruption issue. That advice must\nbe given:\n\n(a) in writing; and\n\n(b) as soon as reasonably practicable after the decision is made.\n\n(10) This Act continues to apply to the head of the law enforcement\nagency, and that agency, in relation to the corruption issue unless\nthe Integrity Commissioner advises otherwise:\n\n(a) in the advice given under subsection (9); or\n\n(b) in a later written advice given to the head of that agency.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-11-sec-12-ss-8"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-11-sec-12-ss-9"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-11-sec-12-ss-10"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "ca47509e43eee3ae70becf30d8b92251e9301d9747c59c6fdca2305b4579578c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-11-sec-12",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "12 At the end of section 32",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\nDeciding to take no further action\n\n(8) The Integrity Commissioner may decide under subsection (2) to\ntake no further action in relation to the corruption issue only if he\nor she is satisfied that:\n\n(a) the corruption issue is already being, or will be, investigated\nby:\n\n(i) a law enforcement agency; or\n\n(ii) a government agency; or\n\n(iii) an integrity agency for a State or Territory; or\n\n(b) the corrupt conduct to which the corruption issue relates has\nbeen, is or will be, the subject of proceedings before a court;\nor\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 11  Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 153, 2015\n\n(c) an investigation of the corruption issue is not warranted\nhaving regard to all the circumstances.\n\n(9) The Integrity Commissioner must advise the head of the law\nenforcement agency of a decision under subsection (2) to take no\nfurther action in relation to the corruption issue. That advice must\nbe given:\n\n(a) in writing; and\n\n(b) as soon as reasonably practicable after the decision is made.\n\n(10) This Act continues to apply to the head of the law enforcement\nagency, and that agency, in relation to the corruption issue unless\nthe Integrity Commissioner advises otherwise:\n\n(a) in the advice given under subsection (9); or\n\n(b) in a later written advice given to the head of that agency."
    },
