    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-11-sec-18",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "18 Subsections 58(1), (2) and (3)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-11-sec-18"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.49",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nAdvice to person who referred issue under section 23\n\n(1) The Integrity Commissioner may advise a person (or a\nrepresentative nominated by the person) of the outcome of an\ninvestigation of a corruption issue raised by the person in a referral\nunder section 23.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 11  Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 153, 2015\n\nManner of giving advice\n\n(2) One way of advising the person (or the representative) is to give a\ncopy of all or part of any report prepared under subsection 54(1) in\nrelation to the investigation.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nAdvice to person who referred issue under section 23\n\n(1) The Integrity Commissioner may advise a person (or a\nrepresentative nominated by the person) of the outcome of an\ninvestigation of a corruption issue raised by the person in a referral\nunder section 23.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 11  Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 153, 2015\n\nManner of giving advice\n\n(2) One way of advising the person (or the representative) is to give a\ncopy of all or part of any report prepared under subsection 54(1) in\nrelation to the investigation.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-11-sec-18-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-11-sec-18-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4f6a8b58960165aedd9abfbaaf82bae89a12523ca4a765199321393f7d7d2e7b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-11-sec-18",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "18 Subsections 58(1), (2) and (3)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 49,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsections, substitute:\nAdvice to person who referred issue under section 23\n\n(1) The Integrity Commissioner may advise a person (or a\nrepresentative nominated by the person) of the outcome of an\ninvestigation of a corruption issue raised by the person in a referral\nunder section 23.\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 11  Australian Commission for Law Enforcement Integrity\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 153, 2015\n\nManner of giving advice\n\n(2) One way of advising the person (or the representative) is to give a\ncopy of all or part of any report prepared under subsection 54(1) in\nrelation to the investigation."
    },
