    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-12-sec-6",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6 After section 24AB",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-12-sec-6"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.53",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n24ABA  Examiner may direct that returnable items be returned\n\n(1) If an examiner conducting an examination is satisfied that a\nreturnable item produced by a person during the examination:\n\n(a) is not required (or is no longer required) for the purposes of\nthe ACC operation/investigation to which the examination\nrelates; or\n\n(b) will no longer be so required once certain conditions (the\nreturn conditions) have been met;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 12  Australian Crime Commission\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 153, 2015\n\nthe examiner may, at or before the time the person is excused or\nreleased from further attendance at the examination, direct that the\nitem be returned to:\n\n(c) the person; or\n\n(d) the owner, if the person is not entitled to possess it.\n\n(2) The direction may specify that the return of the item is subject to\nany return conditions being met.\n\n(3) Members of the staff of the ACC, or any person who has been\npresent at the examination and is in possession of the item, must\ncomply with the direction.\n\n(4) The examiner or the CEO may vary or revoke the direction.",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n24ABA  Examiner may direct that returnable items be returned\n\n(1) If an examiner conducting an examination is satisfied that a\nreturnable item produced by a person during the examination:\n\n(a) is not required (or is no longer required) for the purposes of\nthe ACC operation/investigation to which the examination\nrelates; or\n\n(b) will no longer be so required once certain conditions (the\nreturn conditions) have been met;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 12  Australian Crime Commission\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 153, 2015\n\nthe examiner may, at or before the time the person is excused or\nreleased from further attendance at the examination, direct that the\nitem be returned to:\n\n(c) the person; or\n\n(d) the owner, if the person is not entitled to possess it.\n\n(2) The direction may specify that the return of the item is subject to\nany return conditions being met.\n\n(3) Members of the staff of the ACC, or any person who has been\npresent at the examination and is in possession of the item, must\ncomply with the direction.\n\n(4) The examiner or the CEO may vary or revoke the direction.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-12-sec-6-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-12-sec-6-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-12-sec-6-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-12-sec-6-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d5952378f5b05098fe35b3f893ef3206ffb81abf9394bcbd7bcc22d7c43f0758"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-12-sec-6",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6 After section 24AB",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 53,
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n24ABA  Examiner may direct that returnable items be returned\n\n(1) If an examiner conducting an examination is satisfied that a\nreturnable item produced by a person during the examination:\n\n(a) is not required (or is no longer required) for the purposes of\nthe ACC operation/investigation to which the examination\nrelates; or\n\n(b) will no longer be so required once certain conditions (the\nreturn conditions) have been met;\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nSchedule 12  Australian Crime Commission\n\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\nNo. 153, 2015\n\nthe examiner may, at or before the time the person is excused or\nreleased from further attendance at the examination, direct that the\nitem be returned to:\n\n(c) the person; or\n\n(d) the owner, if the person is not entitled to possess it.\n\n(2) The direction may specify that the return of the item is subject to\nany return conditions being met.\n\n(3) Members of the staff of the ACC, or any person who has been\npresent at the examination and is in possession of the item, must\ncomply with the direction.\n\n(4) The examiner or the CEO may vary or revoke the direction."
    },
