    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-14-sec-11",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "11 Subsection 183(4)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-14-sec-11"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.61",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nApproved examiners\n\n(4) An approved examiner is a person who holds an appointment\nunder this section.\n\n(5) The Minister may appoint as an *approved examiner:\n\n(a) a person who holds an office, or is included in a class of\npeople, specified in the regulations; or\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of\nanother federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State\nor Territory; and\n\n(ii) has been so enrolled for at least 5 years; and\n\n(iii) has indicated to the Minister that the person is willing to\nbe appointed.\n\n(6) An *approved examiner may resign his or her appointment by\ngiving the Minister a written resignation. The resignation takes\neffect on the day it is received by the Minister or, if a later day is\nspecified in the resignation, on that later day.\n\n(7) The Minister may revoke an appointment of an *approved\nexaminer.",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nApproved examiners\n\n(4) An approved examiner is a person who holds an appointment\nunder this section.\n\n(5) The Minister may appoint as an *approved examiner:\n\n(a) a person who holds an office, or is included in a class of\npeople, specified in the regulations; or\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of\nanother federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State\nor Territory; and\n\n(ii) has been so enrolled for at least 5 years; and\n\n(iii) has indicated to the Minister that the person is willing to\nbe appointed.\n\n(6) An *approved examiner may resign his or her appointment by\ngiving the Minister a written resignation. The resignation takes\neffect on the day it is received by the Minister or, if a later day is\nspecified in the resignation, on that later day.\n\n(7) The Minister may revoke an appointment of an *approved\nexaminer.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-14-sec-11-ss-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-14-sec-11-ss-5"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-14-sec-11-ss-6"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-14-sec-11-ss-7"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0244004d9ec640f98332c4c5fcb39e3cf2f0a3967bf5543ad0432055661db2b8"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-14-sec-11",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "11 Subsection 183(4)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 61,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nApproved examiners\n\n(4) An approved examiner is a person who holds an appointment\nunder this section.\n\n(5) The Minister may appoint as an *approved examiner:\n\n(a) a person who holds an office, or is included in a class of\npeople, specified in the regulations; or\n\n(b) a person who:\n\n(i) is enrolled as a legal practitioner of the High Court, of\nanother federal court or of the Supreme Court of a State\nor Territory; and\n\n(ii) has been so enrolled for at least 5 years; and\n\n(iii) has indicated to the Minister that the person is willing to\nbe appointed.\n\n(6) An *approved examiner may resign his or her appointment by\ngiving the Minister a written resignation. The resignation takes\neffect on the day it is received by the Minister or, if a later day is\nspecified in the resignation, on that later day.\n\n(7) The Minister may revoke an appointment of an *approved\nexaminer."
    },
