      "dc:source": "crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(3) Despite subsection (2), an appropriate authorising officer (other\nthan the Commissioner or a Deputy Commissioner) must not vary\nan authority on the authorising officer’s own initiative if doing so\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nControlled operations  Schedule 16\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\nwould have the effect that the controlled operation would be a\nmajor controlled operation by virtue of paragraph 15GD(2)(a).",
      "skos:definition": "Add:\n\n(3) Despite subsection (2), an appropriate authorising officer (other\nthan the Commissioner or a Deputy Commissioner) must not vary\nan authority on the authorising officer’s own initiative if doing so\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nControlled operations  Schedule 16\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\nwould have the effect that the controlled operation would be a\nmajor controlled operation by virtue of paragraph 15GD(2)(a).",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-16-sec-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015-sch-16-sec-5-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8da16e92c53246ce33e2b839d181d7b98df1c2749dc049826a3b73e9493f1471",
      "skos:note": "An authorising officer must not vary an authority on their own initiative."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-legislation-amendment-powers-offences-and-other-measures-act-2015#sch-16-sec-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "5 At the end of section 15GQ",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "Add:\n\n(3) Despite subsection (2), an appropriate authorising officer (other\nthan the Commissioner or a Deputy Commissioner) must not vary\nan authority on the authorising officer’s own initiative if doing so\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2015A00153\n\nControlled operations  Schedule 16\n\nNo. 153, 2015\nCrimes Legislation Amendment (Powers, Offences and Other\nMeasures) Act 2015\n\nwould have the effect that the controlled operation would be a\nmajor controlled operation by virtue of paragraph 15GD(2)(a)."
    },
